# Development-only overrides, kept in the repository as a reference of the
# Ollama setup. The name ends in `.off` on purpose: Pydantic reads `.env.local`,
# not this file, so cloning it changes nothing. To switch the backend to the
# local Ollama, copy it: cp .env.local.off .env.local
#
# Pydantic reads `.env` first and `.env.local` after it, so every variable here
# wins over the official configuration in `.env`. If this file does not exist,
# the backend runs the official configuration: gpt-4o-mini, 5 s, one retry.
#
# The current override is a local Ollama. A cold model (the one Ollama unloads
# after 5 minutes idle) needs about 7 s to load and answer, so the official 5 s
# plus one retry turns the first phrase after an idle into a hard error. Ten
# seconds and zero retries fit that load in one attempt and keep the worst case
# at 10 s, still under the 15 s the Android client waits.
#
# Delete .env.local (or this copy) before a demo with the official model.
LLM_API_KEY=ollama
LLM_MODEL=qwen3:4b-instruct
LLM_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1
LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=10000
LLM_MAX_RETRIES=0
